<title>BELGIUM: Bernheim-Comofi plunges into red in 1996.</title>
<headline>Bernheim-Comofi plunges into red in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit/loss		 160 loss  vs  426 profit</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)	     100	 vs  100</p>
<p>    Net cash flow			   251	 vs  496</p>
<p>NOTE - Bernheim-Comofi is a Belgian property company with a focus on holdings in real estate outside Belgium and car parks.</p>
<p>The company had already warned that 1996 earnings would be negatively influenced by a 375 million franc write down on an investment in Berlin.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
